{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Awaken</b> — by way of parable, the lyre awakens of itself when dawn breaks. And Rabbi Moses said: כי אעירה is a transitive verb, like וירעני." "And the sense of <b>Awaken the lyre</b> — for I shall awaken you at dawn."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 108, :notes {0 "Rabbi Moses = Ibn Ezra's contemporary Moses ben Joseph, likely the Karaite grammarian Moses ben Joseph Tibbon; resolved by inference from Ibn Ezra's usage elsewhere."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:07.213891564Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}